===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
===============================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the code written for this project. It does NOT
cover the two vendored components below, which keep their own copyright and
terms. Both live under src/HuskFilter/ and both arrived through Unity Capture,
which vendors them the same way.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Unity Capture -- src/HuskFilter/HuskFilter.cpp, HuskFilter.def, shared.inl
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Unity Capture
    Copyright (c) 2018 Bernhard Schelling
    Based on UnityCam, Copyright (c) 2016 MHD Yamen Saraiji
    The MIT License (MIT)
    https://github.com/schellingb/UnityCapture

The full notice is reproduced verbatim at the top of each of those files and
must not be removed or rewritten.

Vendored with three changes, all of them naming, all of them so that this
filter and an unmodified Unity Capture can be installed side by side without
reaching each other's clients:

    1. the capture device name       (HuskFilter.cpp)
    2. the four CLSIDs               (HuskFilter.cpp)
    3. the four shared kernel object names -- mutex, two events and the file
       mapping                       (shared.inl)

Change 2 without change 3 would be half a rebranding: two filters with
separate COM registrations still sharing one piece of memory.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Microsoft DirectShow base classes -- src/HuskFilter/streams.h, streams.cpp
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Copyright (c) 1992-2001 Microsoft Corporation.  All rights reserved.

These two files are Microsoft's DirectShow base classes (the BaseClasses
sample that ships with the Windows SDK). streams.cpp is an amalgamation of 21
of the individual BaseClasses source files, each still carrying its own
"// File:" banner and Microsoft copyright notice; there are 28 such notices
across the two files. Together they are 17,603 of the 19,230 lines under
src/HuskFilter/.

They are used unmodified, they are NOT licensed under the MIT grant above, and
they remain subject to the terms under which Microsoft distributes the Windows
SDK samples. The copyright notices inside them must not be removed.
